# Extra specs for the `rocm-gfx90a` flavor (one per line; `#` comments allowed).
# Added via `spack add` on top of the base environment. amdgpu_target=gfx90a
# comes from flavors/rocm-gfx90a.yaml (applied only to packages that expose it).
#
# Upstream Spack's `hip` builds the whole ROCm stack from source — llvm-amdgpu
# (AMD's clang fork), comgr, hsa-rocr-dev, the runtime — which costs hours and
# more disk than a CI runner has. spack_repo/acts/packages/ therefore overrides
# `hip`, `llvm-amdgpu` and `hsa-rocr-dev` with binary packages that unpack AMD's
# own rpms (~307 MB download, ~1.2 GB installed, a couple of minutes). Those
# names are hardcoded in `depends_on` upstream (HIP is not a virtual), which is
# why they are overrides rather than a separate `rocm-bin` package.

# ROCm HIP toolchain. The prefix is a complete /opt/rocm-style root: hipcc,
# clang, the device libraries, the runtime and every CMake config package.
hip

# traccc GPU stack, verified variant names:
#   vecmem  -> its own `+hip` variant     (depends_on hip when +hip)
#   covfie  -> spack ROCmPackage `+rocm`  (NOT +hip; maps to COVFIE_PLATFORM_HIP)
#              ROCmPackage also pulls llvm-amdgpu + hsa-rocr-dev, hence the
#              binary overrides for those two as well.
vecmem +hip
covfie +rocm

